Shoalcade: cheats through retro_cheat_set / retro_cheat_reset for the Dolphin libretro core (GameCube + Wii).
Upstream only switched codes already in the game's INI (and only with "Automatically Import Cheats" on), so a
code typed into Shoalcade did nothing. With this patch:
- retro_cheat_set: a code that isn't one of the INI's codes is added. Lines are joined by '+' (or new lines).
  "AR:" in front = Action Replay, "GECKO:" = Gecko; with neither, dashed lines (XXXX-XXXX-XXXXX) are encrypted
  Action Replay (decrypted with Dolphin's own ARDecrypt) and plain "XXXXXXXX YYYYYYYY" lines are Gecko
  (Shoalcade decision D-4). An unreadable code is skipped (logged). "Internal Cheats" must still be on.
- retro_cheat_reset: drops the added codes and puts the INI's codes back as the INI has them. It no longer
  calls PatchEngine::Shutdown(), which also removed the game's own INI patches (GameSettings fixes).
- retro_unserialize: re-arms the Gecko code handler with the codes on now, so loading a snapshot made with a
  Gecko cheat on doesn't bring that cheat back (Dolphin's own FIXME in Gecko::DoState).
- A title boot (PatchEngine::LoadPatches) applies these lists instead of re-reading the INI's codes, so codes the
  frontend sets before the game has booted (its start-up cheats) aren't dropped (PatchEngine::SetCheatCodesOverride).
Nothing is written to the game's INI, its save or the system folder.

